                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is a maze auto-runner, where you can really only control changing directions.  Each level starts out slower, but speeds up as you go.  The level can be completed once the percentage hits 100%.  If you 'crash' / fail, you have to start each level from the start, which can be brutal.\n\nThere is some type of loose story here, and it has one music track that I'm aware of, that repeats, but it works with the game and the voice over.  The surreal asthetic is also a nice touch, and makes the game its own thing.  I haven't finished it and have only played it in small amounts, but I do find myself coming back to it.\n\nI'd give it a tentative thumbs up, I like it for the style, but it isn't a casual kind of game, you'll need to git gud and there will be some raging.",
